      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The empirical evidence linking facial recognition directly to reduced crime is still highly debated and often anecdotal, rather than conclusive. While deployment systems promise increased threat detection, critics point out that false positives and over-reliance on surveillance can create a false sense of security. True safety improvements often require comprehensive policies and integration with other security measures, not just the technology itself. Therefore, any claim of superior safety must be rigorously evidence-based, not simply based on vendor assurances.",
      "source": "target",
