      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This tension is the core of the ethical debate, where civil liberties advocates argue that a constant, pervasive gaze fundamentally alters the nature of public anonymity. From this perspective, the technology's function *is* the violation, regardless of the purported benefits. Finding a \"balance\" is difficult because the technology operates by normalizing state observation, effectively creating a chilling effect on freedom of movement and assembly. Whether this is an \"extreme view\" depends on one's foundational commitment to privacy versus security in a democratic society.",
